description:
## Context

Plan §4 Phase 6: "Carry Phase 0 defects forward as requirements." Not surface-dependent, so unlike the event-log work it does not wait on the vkh0.2 freeze - it can land early alongside vkh0.3.

Six defects we have already paid for, each of which the replacement must not reintroduce:
- the clock error - updated_at cannot be before created_at - which is what made the gate flaky in 55yh;
- the dependency-field spelling inconsistency;
- the unconfigurable lint templates;
- the single-line acceptance-criteria field;
- ids whose internal hyphens break our own beads-commit-msg gate (the --slug form, see jms0);
- the absolute-path leak in the committed export (vkh0.5).

Each becomes a committed regression test, so the replacement cannot reintroduce a defect we already paid for. This is the repo rule that a dependency defect is requirements input for our own replacement and the proof must become a committed gate - never a fix applied outside this repo.

Plan §3.6 is the governing principle: prefer the root cause when the proximate fix is a workaround, but ship the workaround first when the root cause is a phase away.
